  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "On the number line, point \\(O\\) represents 0 and point \\(A\\) represents 3. Draw a line through \\(A\\) perpendicular to the number line, and choose point \\(B\\) on this line such that \\(AB=2\\). Draw an arc centered at \\(O\\) with radius \\(OB\\), intersecting the positive half of the number line at point \\(P\\). Between which two consecutive integers does the number represented by \\(P\\) lie?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "2 and 3",
    "B": "3 and 4",
    "C": "4 and 5"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(OB^2=3^2+2^2=13\\), so \\(OP=OB=\\sqrt{13}\\). Since \\(3^2=9<13<16=4^2\\), we have \\(3<\\sqrt{13}<4\\).",
